+// Share of the VERTICAL prepaint budget to put ahead of the scroll. 0.5 is
+// upstream's symmetric split, and is the default, so this patch lands as a
+// no-op and can be A/B'd at runtime.
+//
+// WHY IT IS WORTH A KNOB. The budget is (multiplier - 1) x viewport height,
+// and upstream halves it above and below. During a fling only the leading half
+// is ever shown: the trailing half is content the user has already passed.
+// Measured on taimen 2026-09-09 at 1440x2880, one 6-fling drag of a 79000 px
+// article -- raising the multiplier from 2 to 4, which triples the budget and
+// costs 740 -> 1415 MB of tile memory, removed every frame that was more than
+// half unpainted. Moving the SAME budget to the leading side is the cheap half
+// of that: no extra tiles, no extra memory, ~1.5x the lead at 0.75.
+//
+// It is a trade, not free. The trailing prepaint is what makes an immediate
+// reversal cheap, so a value near 1.0 buys a smooth fling and pays for it the
+// moment the user flings back. 0.75 keeps a quarter of the budget behind.
+static float coverLeadFraction()
+{
+    static const float lead = [] {
+        const char* env = getenv("WEBKIT_LAYERS_COVER_LEAD");
+        if (!env || !*env)
+            return 0.5f;
+        auto value = static_cast<float>(atof(env));
+        return (value >= 0.5f && value <= 1.0f) ? value : 0.5f;
+    }();
+    return lead;
+}
